sentences.t:
Urbs antiqua fuit, Tyrii tenuere coloni,
Karthago, Italiam contra Tiberinaque longe
ostia, dives opum studiisque asperrima belli;

sentences.l:
There was an ancient city — Tyrian settlers held it —
Carthage, facing Italy and the Tiber's far-off
mouths, rich in resources and most fierce in the pursuits of war;

A progeny, however, from Trojan blood was being drawn,
she had heard, which would one day overturn the Tyrian citadels;
from this a people, widely ruling and proud in war,
would come for the ruin of Libya: so the Parcae were rolling it.
